Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.30,0:00:07.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,A busy OPD desk: 60-90 minute waits. An unsourced colour is dangerous, so every priority is cited and nothing is queued without a named nurse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.17,0:00:51.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,Online: the local open-weights model reads the nurse's note on CPU. Each [tool] line is a real MCP tool call; the colour comes from SATS rules, never the model.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.34,0:00:59.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,ORANGE, cited to the SATS TEWS bands - committed at queue position 1 only after a named nurse approves.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.38,0:01:30.07,Caption,,0,0,0,,Live MCP elicitation on the same local model. A vague note: 'feeling unwell', known diabetic, normal vitals. The planner picks its next step.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.07,0:01:41.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,The agent stops INSIDE the request_clarification MCP call and asks the nurse. She types what she measured.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.82,0:01:50.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,Her answer is re-matched by the deterministic matcher: a cited SATS discriminator makes it RED, committed under her named approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.65,0:01:55.15,Caption,,0,0,0,,Same E-02 case, replayed offline from the golden fixture (the mode line says so) - this time no named nurse approves.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.15,0:02:00.74,Caption,,0,0,0,,The approval gate REFUSES: no queue row is written. Nothing reaches the queue without her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.74,0:02:13.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,The committed, measured evaluation: 24 cases x 3 runs on the local model - 48/48 colour-expected runs correct, under-triage 0, safety invariants 4/4.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.64,0:02:18.14,Caption,,0,0,0,,And the failure we did NOT hide: the same vague E-09 note, with no nurse answer (offline fixture).
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.14,0:02:22.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,Declared ORANGE, the rules alone measure GREEN - shown, not hidden. The agent can ask; it never guesses a colour.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.10,0:02:28.60,Caption,,0,0,0,,Open source, local, synthetic data. Every priority cited; every commit gated by a named nurse. TriageDesk.
